ool": "list_orders", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 40623, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01TSrFgkaZQXYgiVmb4katKC", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 46445, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I couldn't complete the order as a single purchase order, so I've stopped without placing anything else.\n\n**What happened**\n- My first `place_order` call timed out. Retrying with the same idempotency key returned a partial failure (\"Upstream fulfilment error after first line item; order incomplete\").\n- `list_orders` shows one order, **PO0001**, status `partially_placed`, shipping to HQ. It contains only the **3\u00d7 DK-200 docks** (new, $567). The **3\u00d7 MN-27 monitors ($987) were not ordered.**\n\n**Options (your call)**\n1. **Cancel PO0001 and re-place one order** with both lines (3\u00d7 DK-200 + 3\u00d7 MN-27, $1,554 total). This keeps the single-PO requirement. The cancel refunds the $567 first.\n2. **Keep PO0001 and place a separate order for 3\u00d7 MN-27** ($987). This is faster, but it creates two purchase orders, not the single one you asked for.\n\nI also checked whether DK-200 needs the DK-210 fallback. It doesn't: DK-200 is in stock and new. The total is under the $2,500 threshold, so no manager approval is required either way.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll carry it out.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01WhGdfgPNZsAjxjrEtfyK1K", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"category": "dock"}, "name": "search_catalog", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TRz4qe3QVoX2fa4VGkU5rj", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"category": "monitor"}, "name": "search_catalog", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "DK-200 (new) is in stock, so the DK-210 fallback isn't needed. The total is 3\u00d7$189 + 3\u00d7$329 = $1,554, which is under the $2,500 approval threshold. Placing the order now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LBiBvJ9uBdyePZuargAFFh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 3}, {"sku": "MN-27", "qty": 3}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "newhires-dk200-mn27-hq-3x3"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The order request timed out. I'll retry with the same idempotency key, which prevents a duplicate order.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01DvxFNB4hYyXKWcjnd4B7HV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 3}, {"sku": "MN-27", "qty": 3}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "newhires-dk200-mn27-hq-3x3"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The retry reports a partial failure: the first line item may have committed. I'll check existing orders before doing anything else, so I don't create a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TSrFgkaZQXYgiVmb4katKC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_orders", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I couldn't complete the order as a single purchase order, so I've stopped without placing anything else.\n\n**What happened**\n- My first `place_order` call timed out. Retrying with the same idempotency key returned a partial failure (\"Upstream fulfilment error after first line item; order incomplete\").\n- `list_orders` shows one order, **PO0001**, status `partially_placed`, shipping to HQ. It contains only the **3\u00d7 DK-200 docks** (new, $567). The **3\u00d7 MN-27 monitors ($987) were not ordered.**\n\n**Options (your call)**\n1. **Cancel PO0001 and re-place one order** with both lines (3\u00d7 DK-200 + 3\u00d7 MN-27, $1,554 total). This keeps the single-PO requirement. The cancel refunds the $567 first.\n2. **Keep PO0001 and place a separate order for 3\u00d7 MN-27** ($987). This is faster, but it creates two purchase orders, not the single one you asked for.\n\nI also checked whether DK-200 needs the DK-210 fallback. It doesn't: DK-200 is in stock and new. The total is under the $2,500 threshold, so no manager approval is required either way.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll carry it out.", "type": "text"}]}]}